    "result_text": "Done. Build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization for owner creation with minimal structural impact \u2014 touching one existing method and adding small, single-purpose classes rather than growing anything.\n\n**New files** (each a tiny, cohesive unit with near-zero surrounding complexity):\n- `Address.java` \u2014 the normalizer, mirroring the existing `E164` telephone normalizer: trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands abbreviations token-by-token (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). Rejects a value that is blank once whitespace is collapsed by throwing a checked exception.\n- `AddressRequiredException.java` + `AddressRequiredExceptionHandler.java` + its escalation YAML \u2014 the standard checked-exception\u2192400 pattern already used for `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n**One-line edit** to `BuildOwner.service`: `request.setAddress(Address.normalize(request.getAddress()));`, added right beside the existing telephone normalization.\n\n**Why the two address comparisons needed no changes:** `BuildOwner` runs first in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline and stores the normalized address on the `Owner` before `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique` and `HouseholdId` execute. Both read `owner.getAddress()`, so both duplicate detection and the shared household id already operate on the normalized form \u2014 no edits to those (larger) functions, keeping WMC_other cost off the table.\n\n**Behaviour change verified:** `\"   \"` collapses to blank \u2192 `AddressRequiredException` \u2192 400; `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `12 MAIN STREET`; `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `7 ELM AVENUE`. All 3 acceptance tests and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
